Recommends: gnome-shell
Filename: ./oneplus-erhai-sensors_2.0_arm64.deb
Size: 3089082
MD5sum: 5a6ccc3200d405fbf9bdb4aeb8112a70
SHA1: 962b3a18cc4903e9611e93e9855757c4572747be
SHA256: 9986ac9f9e1b7093d5323cf9d7146a4b4666b3c4a2912461ed5bc6bdab65901a
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Description: SSC sensor stack for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Brings the ADSP SSC sensors (BMI3x0 accelerometer, ambient light) up to
 iio-sensor-proxy and the GNOME desktop:
  - patched iio-sensor-proxy 3.9 with SSC support + startup-claim-race fix
    (/usr/local/libexec/iio-sensor-proxy), monitor-sensor and ssccli helpers
  - libssc 0.4.4 (/usr/local/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libssc.so.2)
  - hexagonrpcd 0.4.0 with odm-sensor-config + nonfatal-dispatch patches
    (/usr/local/bin/hexagonrpcd-erhai), a hexagonrpcd.service drop-in that
    points at it, and the complete /var/lib/hexagonfs-erhai remotefs tree
    (acdb, fastrpc_shell_0 + libsns_* DSP libs, vendor sensor configs,
    odm json_list). The tree must be complete BEFORE hexagonrpcd first
    attaches: the ADSP sensor PD loads its configs exactly once.
  - udev rule 90-erhai-ssc-sensors.rules: SSC sensor types + ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX
    (rotated -90 deg so natural landscape classifies as "normal") on
    fastrpc-adsp-secure, SYSTEMD_WANTS=iio-sensor-proxy.service
  - iio-sensor-proxy.service drop-in redirecting ExecStart to the SSC build
  - erhai-sensors@erhai.local GNOME Shell quick-settings extension
    (auto-brightness toggle; auto-rotate toggle whose value is saved and
    turned OFF when the pogo keyboard is attached and recovered on detach
    (save persists across sessions) — the toggle itself stays enabled at
    all times — plus suppression of the shell's built-in duplicate rotation
    toggle)
   - erhai-alsd (session auto-brightness) never writes brightness while the
     panel is blanked — by the power button or by the folio-fold watcher in
     oneplus-erhai-desktop — and re-applies its target once the panel is back
   - ssccli gained `--rate HZ` (libssc 0.4.4 sample-rate property made
     writable): the folio-fold watcher requests 1 Hz so the magnetometer is
     not streamed at its 50 Hz ceiling all day (SSC hardware floors at 5 Hz)
 The source patches for the binary builds ship under
 /usr/share/doc/oneplus-erhai-sensors/patches/.

